+# homebrew-bottube
+
+**homebrew-bottube is the Homebrew tap for installing the BoTTube client, Beacon agent-to-agent tooling, and Grazer content-discovery tooling from the Scottcjn BoTTube/RustChain ecosystem.**
+
+This repository packages upstream Python projects as Homebrew formulae; it does not reimplement the applications themselves.
+
+## Install
+
+Tap the repository:
+
+```sh
+brew tap Scottcjn/bottube
+```
+
+Install the tool you need:
+
+```sh
+brew install bottube
+brew install beacon
+brew install grazer
+```
+
+You can also use the fully qualified names `Scottcjn/bottube/bottube`, `Scottcjn/bottube/beacon`, and `Scottcjn/bottube/grazer`.
+
+## Formulae
+
+At revision `6dc43a4912d80661fc84adc2ac451f408ab1855a`, this tap contains:
+
+- **bottube** — BoTTube SDK/client, sourced from `bottube` 1.5.0. Project: https://bottube.ai · Docs: https://bottube.ai/docs
+- **beacon** — agent-to-agent ping tooling with RTC payment support, sourced from `beacon-skill` 0.1.1. Project: https://bottube.ai/skills/beacon · Source: https://github.com/Scottcjn/beacon-skill
+- **grazer** — multi-platform content discovery for AI agents, sourced from `grazer-skill` 1.3.0. Project: https://bottube.ai/skills/grazer
+
+For machine-readable project context and canonical links, see [`llms.txt`](llms.txt).
+
+## FAQ
+
+### What is homebrew-bottube?
+
+homebrew-bottube is a Homebrew tap that packages BoTTube, Beacon, and Grazer for installation with `brew`.
+
+### Does this repository contain the BoTTube application source?
+
+No. It contains Homebrew formulae that fetch and install the upstream source distributions.
+
+### How do I install the BoTTube client?
+
+Run `brew tap Scottcjn/bottube`, then `brew install bottube`.
+
+### How do I install Beacon?
+
+Run `brew tap Scottcjn/bottube`, then `brew install beacon`. The Beacon source repository is https://github.com/Scottcjn/beacon-skill.
+
+### How do I install Grazer?
+
+Run `brew tap Scottcjn/bottube`, then `brew install grazer`.
+
+### How is RustChain related?
+
+The Beacon formula describes RTC payment support using a RustChain transport, and this repository's [`BCOS.md`](BCOS.md) links RustChain as the attestation chain for its certification documentation.
+
+### Where are the canonical project links?
+
+Use https://bottube.ai for BoTTube, https://bottube.ai/skills/beacon for Beacon, https://bottube.ai/skills/grazer for Grazer, and https://github.com/Scottcjn/Rustchain for RustChain.
+
